<title>USA: DLJ unit buys stake in Brazil rental firm.</title>
<headline>DLJ unit buys stake in Brazil rental firm.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette said Tuesday its merchant banking fund, DLJ Merchant Banking Partners II, L.P. has invested $48.75 million to acquire a 33.33 percent ownership interest in the Brazilian company,  Localiza Rent A Car S.A., which it said is the leading car rental and fleet management company in South America.</p>
<p>The transaction is the first investment by DLJ Merchant Banking Partners II.</p>
<p>Headquartered in Belo Horizonte, Brazil, Localiza is network of vehicle rental outlets includes 50 company-owned and 287 franchise locations throughout Latin America.</p>
</text>
